 "summary": {
  "version": 2,
  "basis": "em",
  "attribution": "Written by a model from the explanatory memorandum; not the record",
  "describes_version": "original",
  "as_of": "2024-11-25",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would give Commonwealth entities express legislative authority to charge and collect a payment surcharge whenever they already have authority under law to collect the underlying payment.",
   "It would also let the Minister set Commonwealth surcharging policies by legislative instrument, which entities must take all reasonable steps to follow when charging, collecting or refunding surcharges.",
   "The bill would commence the day after Royal Assent and sits with an Imposition Bill and a Consequential Provisions Bill that apply the authority back to 1 January 2003."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "A Commonwealth entity with the power to collect a payment under Commonwealth, state or territory law could charge a surcharge on that payment.",
   "No surcharge could be charged under the bill where the payment is already surchargeable under another law.",
   "Surcharges must not amount to a tax and would be charged on a cost recovery basis to offset the entity's banking costs for the payment method used.",
   "The Minister could make Commonwealth surcharging policies by legislative instrument, subject to sunsetting and disallowance.",
   "An entity could refund a surcharge in whole or in part at its discretion, and failing to follow a policy would not invalidate a surcharge decision.",
   "Decisions to charge, collect or refund a surcharge would not be subject to merits review."
  ],
  "affected": "Commonwealth entities as defined in the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013, the Minister who sets surcharging policy, and people who pay surcharges to those entities are affected.",
